<article class="env-lemma" id="CFCF59">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/CFCF59">Lemma <span data-tag="CFCF59">6.1.4.3</span>.</a> Let $\calX $ and $\calY $ be $\infty $-categories which admit finite limits, let $f: \calX \rightarrow \calY $ be a functor, and let $U_{\bullet }$ be a groupoid object of $\calX $. Suppose that $f$ is left exact at $U_0$. Then $f \circ U_{\bullet }$ is a groupoid object of $\calY $. </p>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This follows immediately from characterization $(4'')$ given in Proposition <a href="/tag/9B195B" data-tag="9B195B">6.1.2.6</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>